  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🗡️ Elven Sword Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Sword names in Tolkien's Elvish, each with what it really means."
    },
    "intro": "Good elven sword names describe the blade in Elvish, the way Tolkien's do. The <a href=\"elf-name-generator.html\">elves</a> of Middle-earth named their <a href=\"sword-name-generator.html\">swords</a>, and the names meant something: <em>Glamdring</em> is \"Foe-hammer\", <em>Orcrist</em> \"Goblin-cleaver\". This **elven sword name generator** builds names the same way, from real words in Tolkien's two Elvish languages, and gives you the meaning of each one. Choose Sindarin, Quenya, Tolkien's own swords, or a mix.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Ten good elven sword names",
        "content": "<p>All ten came from the generator, with the meaning it gives for each:</p><ul><li><strong>Rhîw-crist</strong>: \"Winter-cleaver\". <em>Crist</em> is cleaver, as in Orcrist.</li><li><strong>Thoron-megil</strong>: \"Eagle-sword\". <em>Megil</em> is the Sindarin for sword, as in Mormegil.</li><li><strong>Draug-dring</strong>: \"Wolf-hammer\", with the same <em>-dring</em> as Glamdring.</li><li><strong>Gil-lang</strong>: \"Star-cutlass\". <em>Gil</em> is star, as in Gil-galad.</li><li><strong>Galad-crist</strong>: \"Radiance-cleaver\", for a blade that shines.</li><li><strong>Telpë-macil</strong>: \"Silver-sword\". <em>Macil</em> is the Quenya for sword.</li><li><strong>Isil-macil</strong>: \"Moon-sword\". Isil is the Quenya name for the Moon.</li><li><strong>Laurë-macil</strong>: \"Golden-light-sword\", after the golden light of Laurelin, one of the Two Trees.</li><li><strong>Lómë-lango</strong>: \"Dusk-broadsword\", for an old blade of the Elder Days.</li><li><strong>Ninquë-lango</strong>: \"White-broadsword\", plain and grand.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Tolkien's swords and what their names mean",
